1. Her name is Elia Scolaria, and she is a British VTuber based in England. (Verbatim: "I'm Elia Scolaria, British VTuber... I'm in England right now.")

2. She has a habit of cleaning her PC every few months. (Verbatim: "I clean this PC every few months, I have all the, like, I have the air...")

3. She once found a large number of spiders living inside her old PC. (Verbatim: "I opened it up, and I was like, wow, I got, like, a family living in here... that was my old PC.")

4. She has never replaced the thermal paste on her current PC. (Verbatim: "I haven't replaced the, the, the heat paste ever on this PC...")

5. Her current PC is a few years old. (Verbatim: "how old is this, this PC is a few years old...")

6. She expresses a desire to replace her broken laptop, referred to as "laptop-chan." (Verbatim: "I gotta replace laptop-chan, laptop-chan, RIP, RIP, laptop-chan...")

7. She enjoys sharing fun animal facts, particularly about mosquitoes. (Verbatim: "fun animal fact, by the way, fun, fun animal fact, people get bit by mosquitoes...")

8. She dislikes mosquito bites and finds them unpleasant. (Verbatim: "I don't like mosquito bites...")

9. She believes wristbands are the least effective form of mosquito repellent. (Verbatim: "the least effective mosquito repellent is, is the, is the wristband one.")

10. She is scheduled to play the game *Goose Goose Duck* on Saturday, indicating an interest in it. (Verbatim: "Goose Goose Dock, which I am playing on Saturday.") [end of text]



1. She associates herself with a bunny motif and refers to herself as a bunny. (Verbatim: "I'll be the hardest working bunny in the field.")
2. She has a recurring interest in or aspiration to stream a game called *Bunny Garden*, which currently crashes her PC. (Verbatim: "I will get my Bunny Garden stream. I will. I just need to figure out why. It's Bunny Garden specifically. Bunny Garden breaks my PC.")
3. She received a free sausage roll from YouTube as part of being accepted as a YouTube partner. (Verbatim: "YouTube sent me an email being like, 'You're a YouTube partner. Here, have a sausage roll.'")
4. She prefers a sausage roll over a YouTube Play Button, humorously stating the Play Button isn’t edible. (Verbatim: "You want a YouTube play button? No, sausage roll. Which is fair, 'cause I'll be honest... You can't eat a YouTube play button.")
5. She has a tendency to overthink and over-research simple purchasing decisions, such as buying pillowcases. (Verbatim: "You need to buy pillowcases, okay? You think it'd be simple, just go buy pillowcases. It's not that simple, no. I need to look up and research different fabric type...")
6. She values kindness and forgiveness, and believes in giving people the benefit of the doubt. (Verbatim: "The main thing is, for me, for me, a big thing is just to never villainize anybody... People aren't villains. I like to believe people are good, you know?")
7. She follows a personal principle she calls "rule zero," which is to keep being kind. (Verbatim: "I'm just gonna... I'm just gonna keep following rule zero. Just keep being being kind.")
8. She has technical difficulties with PC performance, particularly games running at uncapped frame rates causing issues. (Verbatim: "I think maybe the frame rate isn't capped or something. 'Cause I had a similar issue with the frog detective.")
9. She expresses difficulty making decisions and dislikes the effort involved in upgrading her computer. (Verbatim: "I'm also not very good at making decisions. I'm the kind of person... I don't wanna go with the effort of replacing computer. It's just a lot of effort.")
10. She humorously claims to have dreamed of receiving a YouTube Play Button, which she says tasted like metal when she ate it. (Verbatim: "Not that I have one from a dream I had. They're surprisingly heavy... Honestly, it just tasted kind of like metal.") [end of text]



1. She sees herself as an anime girl whose purpose is to bring joy to people. (Verbatim: "I am just an anime girl who wants to bring people joy. Nothing more complicated. It's just that simple.")  
2. She believes people are inherently not bad, just flawed and human. (Verbatim: "I don't think people are bad. I think people are just people. We all suck.")  
3. She embraces imperfection and encourages others to accept being imperfect together. (Verbatim: "So, let's be trash, but be trash together.")  
4. She is currently in England. (Verbatim: "That's not true for catching me though. I'm back. I'm back in England.")  
5. She has a slime as a companion or pet. (Verbatim: "Yeah, I've been hanging with the slime.")  
6. She had an afternoon tea with her slime and considers it a wonderful experience. (Verbatim: "There's one that I didn't post that I needed to have a wonderful afternoon tea that we had together.")  
7. She was previously self-conscious about showing her arms due to fear of judgment. (Verbatim: "For real, I was so scared to show my arms. I don't know, like what, I don't know. I feel like people might have judged my arms or something.")  
8. She describes her arms as thin and lacking muscle, jokingly calling them "noodle arms" or "spaghetti-er." (Verbatim: "They're noodle arms, they're very... There's no muscle or anything. It's just straight up spaghetti-er.")  
9. She has little body hair, only on her head, and finds it noteworthy. (Verbatim: "I don't have a lot of, there's not a lot, like, in terms of hair, it's just the hair on my head.")  
10. She refers to her audience as "vtrooper wifu," indicating a playful, affectionate community name. (Verbatim: "You're the best vtrooper wifu ever and you can't change my mind.") [end of text]



